\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Theorem\nonbreakingspace \ref {thm:corankone} at $(4,3)$. The ratios $p_c$ of \eqref  {eq:pvars} have co-weighted mean $1/k$ by \eqref  {eq:pnorm}. Left: the largest $p_{c_0}$ is at least the $t$-weighted mean $\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _ct_cp_c$, so by \eqref  {eq:corankone} its complement dominates. Right: when $p$ is constant every $p_c$ equals $1/k$, the tie law \eqref  {eq:tielaw} holds, every $k$-subset dominates and none dominates strictly.}}{20}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
