\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Lemma\nonbreakingspace \ref {lem:spanning} as a fit. By \eqref  {eq:residual} the slack $\sigma -\zeta ^{\mathsf  {T}}\Omega ^{-1}\zeta $ is the $t$-weighted squared residual of $\hat  \ell $ against the linear functional $\langle \eta ,\xi \rangle $, $\xi :=\Omega ^{-1}\zeta $; disc area is the weight, and an atom under the fitted plane carries a dashed segment. Left: an all-heavy design at $(5,2)$. There $\det \Psi <0$, so $\Psi $ is indefinite, and the trace taken in the proof, rather than a sign for $\Psi $ itself, is what supplies a direction nonnegative for $\Psi $. Right: the trine of Example\nonbreakingspace \ref {ex:trine2}, where $\hat  \ell $ vanishes identically and the fit is exact.}}{33}{figure.10}\protected@file@percent }
